  "gamma": 0.99,
  "rewardNoise": {
    "distribution": "gaussian",
    "mean": 0,
    "sigma": 0.5,
    "appliedTo": "the reward passed to agent.remember() at every env step (training only); the environment, its termination and the true reward are unchanged",
    "stream": "own seeded stream, independent of env starts, exploration and replay sampling: mulberry32(seed * 7919 + 101), one standard normal per env step by Box-Muller (two uniforms per draw, cosine branch). The k-th env step of a run receives the same noise draw for dqn and double-dqn at equal seed.",
    "sigmaJustification": "Set from the reward function alone, no trial run: rewards are +1 on success and -0.05 otherwise. Under the optimal policy (always +0.15) from starts uniform[0, 0.4], episodes last 3, 4 or 5 steps (probabilities 0.375, 0.375, 0.25; 3.875 steps on average), so the pooled per-step reward has mean 0.221 and standard deviation 0.459 (exact, from nav1dStep). sigma = 0.5 is that per-step standard deviation rounded up to one significant digit, about half the reward range (1.05) and ten times the -0.05 step penalty."
  },
